I'm not completely sure what you're trying here, but using the model with free means/variances with suitable anchor items is a possible good start. To evaluate DIF using this approach you would just need to loop over each item and free the parameters for each respective item, and likely apply some family-wise error adjustment for the exploratory data snooping. This is actually what's automated in the DIF() function when using the 'drop' scheme. For this reason I'll avoid running your code below since I believe it's unnecessary.

